        "id": 3661524
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T16:29:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "2048 SkPaths retained process-wide with no byte budget; a single map tile or chart path can be hundreds of KB of verbs/points, so this can hold tens to hundreds of MB with no purge path. Also the global fMutex at L1042/L1059 is taken on every non-volatile path draw on every raster thread.",
      "revId": "d1831165aff28c8dbc7e6bccbf319869edb17863",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
